# =====================================================================
# NEVER-COMMIT PATHS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repository is intended to become publicly visible. Everything not
# excluded here is treated as public. See CLAUDE.md, "Public repo vs.
# internal working files", for the full ruleset and the audit process.
#
# WARNING: .gitignore is not a security boundary. It prevents accidental
# staging; it does NOT protect anything already committed, and it can be
# overridden with `git add -f`. The pre-commit hook in .githooks/ is the
# actual enforcement layer. Neither protects git history retroactively.
# =====================================================================

# Internal working files: planning notes, named private contacts,
# funding strategy, anything not fit for public reading. Never committed.
internal/

# Local-only Claude Code memory access shortcut.
# This is a directory junction pointing to a machine-specific, user-specific
# path (C:\Users\<you>\.claude\projects\...\memory\) that differs between
# machines. Never commit it — each machine creates its own local junction.
# See CLAUDE.md, "Claude's memory: what's in the repo vs. outside it".
.claude-memory

# Microsoft Word lock/owner files (created while a .docx is open).
~$*

# OS and editor cruft
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode cache, generated by running anything in tools/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
